%description:
Tests the dielectric loss of DielectricObstacleLoss: one transmission crosses a
single slab of concrete (resistivity 100 Ohm m, relative permittivity 4.5) that is
0.2 m thick, at two frequencies. Reflection loss is switched off.

The loss is a power factor. A plane wave in a lossy dielectric loses power as
exp(-2 alpha z) with alpha = k sqrt((sqrt(1 + tan(delta)^2) - 1) / 2), where k is the
wave number of the lossless material (c / sqrt(4.5) is the speed in the slab) and
tan(delta) = 1 / (2 pi f rho eps_r eps_0). Expected values:

  2.4 GHz: tan(delta) = 0.01664, k = 106.70 1/m, loss 1.542 dB
  10 MHz:  tan(delta) = 3.994,   k = 0.4446 1/m, loss 0.964 dB

The code before the repair used exp(-2 atan(tan(delta)) k z), which gives 3.085 dB
at 2.4 GHz, twice the exponent of the power decay, and 1.024 dB at 10 MHz.

%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%file: test.ned
import inet.environment.common.PhysicalEnvironment;
import inet.physicallayer.wireless.common.medium.RadioMedium;
import inet.test.unittest.lib.ObstacleLossTest;

network ObstacleLossTestNetwork
{
    submodules:
        physicalEnvironment: PhysicalEnvironment;
        radioMedium: RadioMedium;
        test: ObstacleLossTest;
}
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%file: environment.xml
<environment>
    <object position="min 4.9 -5 -5" orientation="0 0 0" shape="cuboid 0.2 10 10" material="concrete"/>
</environment>
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%inifile: omnetpp.ini
[General]
network = ObstacleLossTestNetwork
ned-path = .;../../../../src;../../lib
cmdenv-express-mode = false
cmdenv-event-banners = false
cmdenv-log-prefix = "%l %C: "
**.cmdenv-log-level = INFO

*.physicalEnvironment.spaceMinX = -10m
*.physicalEnvironment.spaceMinY = -10m
*.physicalEnvironment.spaceMinZ = -10m
*.physicalEnvironment.spaceMaxX = 20m
*.physicalEnvironment.spaceMaxY = 10m
*.physicalEnvironment.spaceMaxZ = 10m
*.physicalEnvironment.config = xmldoc("environment.xml")
*.radioMedium.backgroundNoise.power = -100dBm
*.radioMedium.obstacleLoss.typename = "DielectricObstacleLoss"
*.radioMedium.obstacleLoss.enableReflectionLoss = false

*.test.frequencies = "2.4e9 1e7"
*.test.txX = 0m
*.test.txY = 0m
*.test.txZ = 0m
*.test.rxX = 10m
*.test.rxY = 0m
*.test.rxZ = 0m
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%extraargs: -s
%subst: /\n<!> No more events, simulation completed.*?\n//
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%postrun-command: grep "obstacle loss at" test.out > filtered.out
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%contains: filtered.out
INFO (ObstacleLossTest)ObstacleLossTestNetwork.test: obstacle loss at 2.4e+09 Hz: 1.542 dB
INFO (ObstacleLossTest)ObstacleLossTestNetwork.test: obstacle loss at 1e+07 Hz: 0.964 dB
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%not-contains: stdout
undisposed object:
%not-contains: stdout
-- check module destructor
